    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d312">

                <pb facs="0488" n="174" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg174"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé d’Affaires in
                        China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-20T17:00:00-05:00">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">August 20, 1914, 5 p.m.</hi>
                    </date>
                </dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract]</p>
                <p>Your telegram of August 20, 3 a.m. Inform Minister Liang that the Department
                    regrets its inability to comply with his request.... The Department feels sure
                    that such a course would do more to provoke than to avert war.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
